Provenance of this vendored copy (measurement record:
AGENT_CONTEXT/TASKS/m5-p0-6-path-b.md in the Agenthu repository):

1. Base. The files in this package were re-derived in October 2026 from
   the thu-info-app monorepo (packages/thu-info-lib,
   https://github.com/thu-info-community/thu-info-app) at commit
   06dc3cf0 (2024-07-10 14:53 +0800), the last snapshot under the MIT
   license before the upstream project switched to the Business Source
   License 1.1 (33fd0a86, 2024-07-10 15:07 +0800; Change Date
   2030-09-15). utils/error.ts, the constants in constants/strings.ts,
   and the structural base of lib/core.ts come from that snapshot.

2. Repository-authored work on top of the base, published under the same
   MIT license:
   - utils/network.ts is rewritten for this repository: the request path
     is an injectable platformFetch transport (Tauri / Rust reqwest),
     cookie handling is delegated to the platform cookie jar, and the
     charset policy is UTF-8 only.
   - lib/core.ts carries this repository's authentication adaptation:
     SM2 password encryption (the school login pages now publish an
     #sm2publicKey and accept only encrypted submissions; implemented
     with the sm-crypto package), the OAuth landing flow, the
     oauth lbredirect wrapper for roaming redirects, TOTP as a third
     two-factor option, the device-trust finger3 capture, the
     login-chain reset hook (clearOutstandingLogin), and the
     direct-connect secondary-timetable URL.
   - The package is deliberately narrowed to authentication
     (login / roam / csrf); data clients are not vendored here.

3. Boundary statement. Code from post-BSL upstream commits is NOT
   incorporated by copy. Capabilities the school introduced after the
   MIT boundary (SM2-encrypted submissions, the oauth lbredirect
   entry, TOTP verification) are implemented independently from the
   observable school protocol; residual resemblance is limited to
   protocol facts (element ids, action names, the "04" SM2 prefix)
   that admit no alternative expression.

